WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 line:92%
-I'm so, so happy you are here.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.135 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.503
-And I want to start
by saying there was a moment --

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been a big fan
of your music for long time.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
But there was a moment
where I felt a real connection

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
with you that I never felt
before which is,

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:13.079
you were on "American Idol"
and Kelly Clarkson sang a song,

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Piece by Piece."
-Mnh. Yeah.

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.083 line:92%
-And it was -- she cried,

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.119 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Jennifer Lopez cried,

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:21.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
you cried the hardest.
-Well, yeah.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:22.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if the hardest,
but --

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:25.859
-Except for me at home watching.
-You got it, too.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-I cried so hard.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my wife was making
so much fun of me.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How so?
-She was like,

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You're the worst.
Anything emotional, you cry."

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:34.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like, "Hey,
your boyfriend Keith Urban" --

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
she's a big fan --
"is also crying.

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.172 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Let me off the hook."

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you -- did you --
were you aware

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.876
as you were listening to that
like, "Oh, man, this is on TV."

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. It was everything.
-Yeah.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was the song.
It was the situation.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's pregnant. It's like --
-Yeah.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.550 size:78% position:39%
-It was amazing song.
-It was amazing song.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's a lot going on
in that song.

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.653
-Yeah, I was very jealous you
got to be there for it because

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.488
I thought that was pretty great.
-Well, evidentially,

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.058
you experienced it at home.
-I did. I just want you to know

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we were going through
something very similar.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:03.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, hey, you are about to
go on a 58-city tour.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That must be exciting.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:05.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I'm looking forward
to it.

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
New music
and getting out touring.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love touring.
-Is it great?

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How's your -- I know you --
obviously,

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
you got a couple kids now.
You got a family.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:17.143
Has your touring schedule
changed the way you do it?

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.612 size:84% position:42%
-A little bit maybe.
Go out on the weekends,

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thursday, Friday, Saturday,
sort of three shows.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe a midweek one
occasionally.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I pretty much play shows
and go home,

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:27.787 size:88% position:44%
play shows and go home.
-Your girls are 7 and 9.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:28.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
-7 and 9.
-It's obviously happening

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
during the summer,
a good chunk of this tour.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
Will they -- Do they
like to go out?

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.527
Is that an age where they
like to see you onstage?

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They love the tour bus.
-Okay.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.664
-They love the bunks
and the whole thing in the bus.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:41.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
So -- but, you know,
I have catering at my shows.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:44.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mom has like craft services
at her set.

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:45.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So it's always battle

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:47.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
for who's got the better food.
-Gotcha.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So it's not really like,

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, my God.
Our mom is Nicole Kidman.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:54.180
She's this an amazing actor.
And our dad is Keith Urban."

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Definitely not.
-They don't care about that?

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:57.016 size:75% position:38%
-No, definitely not.
-They're just like,

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Who has the macaroni
and cheese?"

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We had -- She was at a show
of mine one time.

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:03.690 size:78% position:39%
She must have been 6.
A Sunday, she was 6.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we're backstage
and I'm like --

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:07.327 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And they had stayed up.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:08.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
Normally they go to bed early.
You know?

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:09.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they're up.
We go onstage.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "do you want
to come see me play?"

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:12.966 line:92%
She goes, "Do I have to?"

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:13.566 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:14.767 line:92%
Just really keeping it real.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:18.404
-It's also -- I love that
what's keeping her from going to

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
see you at a giant arena
is like,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Dad, it's just --
there is a bus."

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:23.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Totally.
-Yeah like, "I'd love to go.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:25.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I got this bus
to do stuff on."

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:26.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
We played stagecoach

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the weekend and they wanted
to hang in the bus

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
instead of come see Dad play.
So I get it.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Alright, that's alright.
-I totally get it.

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:32.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm glad that happens
for all dads.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sure when you have a 7-
and 9-year-old,

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's happening around
the world.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:40.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
And your wife, Nicole,
sings backup one of the songs

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
on this album?
-Yeah, on "Female." Yes.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:44.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And is it hard to convince
her to do that?

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Oh, it is? Okay.

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:46.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:49.235
It will be like trying to get me
to do a scene in something.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not my comfort level
at all.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.572 line:92%
We have a studio at the house.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:55.441
And it was just one of those
times when I was recording

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
that song "Female,"
and I thought,

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:58.845
if there ever was a song
for her, that's the perfect one.

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was home, so --
-Oh, that's great.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I dragged her down to do it.
-So at least there,

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.050 line:92%
that's the privacy of your home.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.119
But you actually got her
to come up onstage with you

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:09.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Nashville recently.
-Reluctantly she did, yes.

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-And well, what was happened

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
was, I was talking about
this song called

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:14.494
"Parallel Line," which is
on my new album and --

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.997 line:92%
-Got some fans right there.

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.232 line:92%
-So cut a long story short,

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
wasn't planning on singing
the song.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.469
I was playing solo. And I was
going to do some other song.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:27.507
And I'm talking about this song
to try and avoid singing it,

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:28.775 size:78% position:39% line:92%
this particular song.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.877 line:92%
And from the back of the people,

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:33.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hear this woman go,
"Play the song."

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:34.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
And of course, it's Nic.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.683 line:92%
And I'm like, ugh! You know?

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:39.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I thought,
"Well, I'll just say to her,

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.355
'You come up and sing it with
me, and I'll do the song.'

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.924
and that would be the end
of the song. And I can move on."

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.426 line:92%
And I -- some time went by,

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:49.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I saw her slinking slowly
up towards the stage.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:50.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she came up.
-Oh, that's great.

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
-To her credit, she came up
and played it with me.

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That must have been
a real thrill for everybody

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the house that night.
-Me most of all, yes.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:04:00.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What is a recording studio
in your house like?

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is the scene like
when you go to

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.343 line:92%
Keith Urban's recording studio?

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:07.380
-It's pretty chill. We built the
studio with these big windows.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.015 size:81% position:41%
It was supposed to be
an underground studio,

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:11.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is a whole other story.
But it's aboveground,

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.720
has big windows,
lots of natural light coming in.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.956
And I just -- I feed off
that energy really, really well.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
This record "Graffiti U"
is very buoyant.

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.960
It's very up. And I think
part of that is from that.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:24.297
-It would have been completely
different album if you had...

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:25.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-...recorded it underground.

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, underground.
Quite literally, yes.

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yes, yes.

